    "result_text": "All 22 test classes are the `Cp##Tests` acceptance suite; all 33 tests pass.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the `bulkSignupWarning` rule on `POST /api/owners`: when more than 80 owners have already been created on the current business day, the created-owner response includes `bulkSignupWarning: true`; otherwise `false`.\n\nFollowing the project's OfficeFloor function-injection conventions, the change is:\n\n1. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added a `bulkSignupWarning` boolean (readOnly) property to the `Owner` DTO schema, so the generated `OwnerDto` and Jackson serialization pick it up.\n\n2. **`model/Owner.java`** \u2014 added a `@Transient boolean bulkSignupWarning` field (primitive, defaults to `false`) with `isBulkSignupWarning()`/`setBulkSignupWarning()`. It's a create-time signal, not an intrinsic owner attribute, so it's never persisted \u2014 matching how the test reads it back via `GET` (a reloaded owner reports the `false` default).\n\n3. **`function/owner/AssignBulkSignupWarning.java`** \u2014 new pipeline step that counts existing owners whose `registrationDate` equals the business-day-adjusted current date (mirroring the existing `EnsureDailyLimit` accumulation) and sets the flag to `count > 80`. It runs before `save`, so the new owner isn't counted.\n\n4. **`officefloor/rest/api/owners.POST.yml`** \u2014 wired `assignBulkSignupWarning` (with `govern: [ transaction ]`) between `assignNamesakeCount` and `save`.\n\nMapStruct auto-maps the field by name (verified in the generated `OwnerMapperImpl`: `ownerDto.setBulkSignupWarning(owner.isBulkSignupWarning())`), so both the create response and `GET` carry a non-null boolean.\n\nThe new `Cp22Tests`, the related `Cp19Tests` (daily-limit), and the full suite (33 tests) all pass.",
